From 3f8902d238471afcedf3f3180accc9ebb41bbc06 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mshresponse <9147626+mshresponse@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 13:55:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Use the report type metadata syntax Salesforce actually
 emits
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three deploys failed because report type metadata uses a different name space
than describe does, and I kept feeding it describe names. Resolved by building
one report type in the UI and retrieving it, which is what I should have done
first.

  <relationship>   the CHILD OBJECT API NAME
                   StnryAssetCrbnFtprnt, not CarbonFootprints

  <table>          OBJECT API NAMES chained per hop
                   StnryAssetEnvrSrc.StnryAssetCrbnFtprnt.StnryAssetEnrgyUse

  lookup column    the RELATIONSHIP NAME with no Id suffix
                   ParentEnvironmentalSource, not ParentEnvironmentalSourceId

  multi-level      nested <join> elements, inner element is the deeper hop

Report type metadata never uses child relationship names. The describe values
that took two rounds to obtain — CarbonFootprints, StationaryAssetEnergyUses —
are correct for SOQL and useless here.

Also restores the required dashboard titleSize, which the regeneration dropped.

Verified against the org's own schema: 37 files well-formed, every object,
field, relationship, table hop and column reference resolves, no dangling
report type or report references, manifest parity, and a clean source convert.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
